-- title:
--   Reciprocity for the cyclic octic subextension of a GL₂(𝔽₃)-extension
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, let `c8H e` be the subgroup of those $\gamma$ whose image $e\gamma$ is the reduction of a matrix lying in the fixed set $C_8$, and write $K' = L^{\,\mathrm{c8H}\, e}$ for the corresponding intermediate field of $L/\mathbb{Q}$, whose relative Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K')$ is assumed commutative. Fix $\zeta \in \mathbb{C}$ with $\zeta^4 = -1$, an ideal $\mathfrak{f}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$, and an element $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K')$ such that every element of that group lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$. Assume: (i) for every prime carrier $i$, i.e. every element of the set `primeCarriers` of classes in the group of elements coprime to $\mathfrak{f}$ represented by `primeUnit` of a height-one prime $v \nmid \mathfrak{f}$, a datum $D_i$ of type `ArtinFieldCore` is given, consisting of number fields $E_i \subseteq N_i \subseteq \Theta_i$ over $K'$ with $N_i/E_i$ and $\Theta_i/E_i$ Galois with commutative groups, $\Theta_i$ generated over $E_i$ by a primitive $q_i$-th root of unity, a modulus $\mathfrak{m}_i$ of $K'$ divisible by $\mathfrak{f}$, a prime $v_i$ of $K'$ representing $i$ and coprime to $\mathfrak{m}_i$, a prime $w_i$ of $E_i$ above $v_i$ of inertia degree one and coprime to $\mathfrak{m}_i \mathcal{O}_{E_i}$, with $(q_i) \mid \mathfrak{m}_i\mathcal{O}_{E_i}$, together with the further data of that structure; (ii) for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ not dividing $\mathfrak{f}$, the inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ of the prime `primeOver (c8H e) v` of $\mathcal{O}_L$ above $v$ is trivial; (iii) a crossing condition: for all carriers $i, j$ there are $b$ in $(D_i).\mathrm{Ip}$, the group of elements coprime to $\mathfrak{m}_i\mathcal{O}_{E_i}$, and $b'$ in $(D_j).\mathrm{Ip}$ whose images under the maps $(D_i).\mathrm{Ni}$, $(D_j).\mathrm{Ni}$ (relative norm to $K'$ followed by the inclusion from modulus $\mathfrak{m}$ to modulus $\mathfrak{f}$) coincide, and with $(D_i).\omega_{pi}(b) = \sigma$; (iv) for each $i$, `SecondInequalityCTM` for $N_i/E_i$ at $\mathfrak{m}_i\mathcal{O}_{E_i}$, i.e. the index of the subgroup generated by the narrow ray subgroup together with the image of the relative norm from $N_i$ divides $\#\mathrm{Gal}(N_i/E_i)$; (v) for each $i$ and each intermediate field $F$ of $N_i/E_i$ with $[F:E_i]$ prime, the corresponding `FirstInequalityCTM`, i.e. $\#\mathrm{Gal}(F/E_i)$ divides that index for $F/E_i$; (vi) the same two inequalities for $L/K'$ at $\mathfrak{f}$. Let finally $\alpha \in \mathcal{O}_{K'}$ be nonzero with $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak{f}$ and $\tau(\alpha) > 0$ for every ring homomorphism $\tau : K' \to \mathbb{R}$. Then the ray symbol $\prod_v (\mathrm{artinValue}\, e\, h\zeta \, v)^{\,\mathrm{count}_v}$ of the principal fractional ideal $(\alpha)$, formed from the character values `artinValue e hζ` at the finite places of $K'$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the reciprocity step in Artin's derivation of his reciprocity law by crossing the given abelian extension with cyclotomic auxiliary extensions, here for the cyclic octic extension $L/K'$ cut out by the subgroup `c8H e` of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, with the two index inequalities of class field theory taken as hypotheses rather than proved. It supplies the vanishing of the ray symbol on totally positive generators congruent to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak{f}$, and is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.P2.raySymbol_artinValue_span_eq_one_of_artinPairCore`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.P2.raySymbol_artinValue_span_eq_one_of_artinPairCore) on the way to realising the octic character as a Hecke character in the Langlands–Tunnell input.
